{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 23 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D8"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the carboplatin shortage on 2023-04-28 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E32", "D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Accord Healthcare product on the shortage list is manufactured by Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited, a registered plant on the label.",
      "cites": ["E21", "E22"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1191818 of Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited ended 2022-12-02 and was classified OAI, with the classification letter dated 2023-04-05.",
      "cites": ["E17", "D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The OAI classification letter came 23 days before FDA posted the shortage on 2023-04-28.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Subsequent FDA actions included an Import Alert 66-40 listing on 2023-06-01 and a Warning Letter on 2023-07-28 for the same firm.",
      "cites": ["E19", "E18", "D5", "D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale Lakeside site holds only 1 vial of the Teva 60 mL presentation (NDC 00703-4239-01) with 0.67 vials used daily, giving about 1.5 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["E6", "D10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The highest-ranked rule option is to transfer 3 vials of the 10 mg/mL 60 mL vial from Corvale East to Corvale Lakeside, which would raise Lakeside to roughly 4 days of supply while East retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D10"]
    }
  ]
}
